  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Eastern Air Express has $224M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Eastern Air Express won 61 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.7M and obligations that are up 3870.1% year over year. Eastern Air Express shows a sharp jump from prior years: obligations were $0 in FY21, $3.3K in FY22, $2.9M in FY23, $2.2M in FY24, and $5.6M in FY25. The Department of Homeland Security is the dominant buyer, obligating $216M to Eastern Air Express in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $5.6M and the Department of the Interior obligated $3M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations. These figures include contract obligations rather than total contract values for the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables. The concentration of obligations with one agency and the scale of the year-over-year increase are the defining features of Eastern Air Express's FY2026 federal activity.",
